guidebook.section.mob.bear.name=Bear
guidebook.section.mob.bear.desc=Bears are ferocious hunters and will attack almost anything on sight.\nBe wary not to hold food around them.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.polarbear.name=Polar Bear
guidebook.section.mob.polarbear.desc=Polar Bears are as ferocious, if not more, than their brown cousins.\nThey can be found in colder biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.bird.name=Bird
guidebook.section.mob.bird.desc=Birds come in many varieties and love seeds of all kind.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.boar.name=Boar
guidebook.section.mob.boar.desc=Boars, much like their pink cousins, are a valuable source of food.\nBe wary of their nasty temper!\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.bunny.name=Bunny
guidebook.section.mob.bunny.desc=Bunnies are a docile and fluffy animal known for their ability to jump.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.deer.name=Deer
guidebook.section.mob.deer.desc=Deer are another valuable source of food, however they are known to flee at the first sight of danger.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.duck.name=Duck
guidebook.section.mob.duck.desc=Ducks, much like Chickens, are a source of feather. They are thought to be derived from Chickens and are commonly confused for them.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.fox.name=Fox
guidebook.section.mob.fox.desc=Foxes are known to attack smaller prey such as foul and bunnies.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.arcticfox.name=Arctic Fox
guidebook.section.mob.arcticfox.desc=Much like thieir orange cousins, Arctic Foxes hunt for small prey and love to dive into snow.\nThey can be found in colder biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.horse.name=Horse
guidebook.section.mob.horse.desc=Horses make excellent transportation on land, yet are feisty unless tamed.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.pegasus.name=Pegasus
guidebook.section.mob.pegasus.desc=Pegasi, much like their land cousins, make excellent transportation.\nThey are slower but their wings allow them to fly.\nThey can be found rarely in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.unicorn.name=Unicorn
guidebook.section.mob.unicorn.desc=Unicorns make excellent transportation on land.\nThey are the fastest land horse.\nThey can be found rarely in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.kitty.name=Kitty
guidebook.section.mob.kitty.desc=Kitties are small, yet adorable predators that hunt foul.\nMuch like wolves they can be tamed with fish.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.bigcat.name=Big Cat
guidebook.section.mob.bigcat.desc=Lions, tigers, panthers and their kin are apex predators that hunt whatever is smaller than them.\nCubs can be won over with food, but only while they are young.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.rat.name=Rat
guidebook.section.mob.rat.desc=Rats scurry in the dark and swarm to defend one another.\nThey can be found underground and in unlit places.
guidebook.section.mob.rat_hell.name=Hell Rat
guidebook.section.mob.rat_hell.desc=A larger cousin of the rat, at home in fire and unbothered by it.\nThey can be found in the Nether.
guidebook.section.mob.mouse.name=Mouse
guidebook.section.mob.mouse.desc=Mice flee from anything that moves and can be picked up by hand.\nThey are a favourite meal of cats.\nThey can be found in most biomes.
guidebook.section.mob.dolphin.name=Dolphin
guidebook.section.mob.dolphin.desc=Dolphins come in six colours, and the rarer ones swim considerably faster.\nFeed one raw fish until it warms to you, then ride it; look where you want to go and it will dive.\nA pair of tame adults fed cooked fish, left alone together, will raise a calf whose colour is drawn from both parents.\nThey can be found in open water.
guidebook.section.mob.shark.name=Shark
guidebook.section.mob.shark.desc=Sharks hunt anything sharing their water, players included, and eat the leavings afterwards.\nThere is no befriending a wild one, though a shark raised from an egg will spare you.\nThey can be found in open water.
guidebook.section.mob.fishy.name=Lil' Fish
guidebook.section.mob.fishy.desc=Small fish that shoal with their own kind and feed most things larger than themselves.\nOne of the ten varieties is a piranha, and it is not friendly.\nThey can be found in most water.
guidebook.section.mob.shark_egg.name=Shark Egg
guidebook.section.mob.shark_egg.desc=An egg case left behind by a full-grown shark.\nIt hatches after a long soak, and the pup comes out tame.\nOut of the water, nothing happens at all.
guidebook.section.mob.fishy_egg.name=Fishy Egg
guidebook.section.mob.fishy_egg.desc=A clutch of roe dropped by a lil' fish.\nLeft underwater it hatches into a fry of the same variety as its parent, which is how a fished-out lake restocks itself.
